// RUN: check
// COMPILE-FAIL
// EXPECT-EXIT: 65
// CHECK-ERR: Unknown type 'var'.
//
// Chapter 02 coverage: Kinglet has no `var` keyword. The lexer/parser treat
// it as an ordinary (unknown) type name, so `var c = ...;` fails at the
// checker with K1001, not with a dedicated "no var keyword" diagnostic.
// The correct inference keyword is `auto` (see auto_without_initializer.kl
// and definite_assignment_simple.kl for `auto`'s behavior).

int main() {
  var c = 1 + 2;
  return c;
}
